  "title": "Sign-in gets easier to add and use",
  "summary": "Sign-in takes fewer steps, agents get sandboxes, uploads get a privacy option, and five community apps join the catalog.\n\nThe interactive API docs gained Pollinations Connect, so readers can authorize their account and try requests without pasting a key. Plain HTML pages can now add sign-in with the `<polli-connect>` component, without a build step. Smaller docs navigation and loading fixes accompanied the changes.\n\nA Quest contribution added Machines MCP tools for creating, connecting to, pausing and managing Linux sandboxes, running commands, and reading or writing files. The API reference now covers sandbox routes and pricing, with a follow-up correcting its guide link and reference validation.\n\nMedia uploads gained opt-in image metadata stripping through `safe=privacy`, while preserving orientation and colour profile; the upload reference was updated to match. DeepSeek V4.1 Flash gained Quest Pollen access and remote image URL handling as its primary route moved to Azure, with Fireworks as fallback.",
